@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/world/simulation#> .
@prefix actuation: <http://example.org/orexis/actuation#> .
@prefix reporting: <http://example.org/orexis/reporting#> .
@prefix market: <http://example.org/orexis/market#> .
@prefix progression: <http://example.org/orexis/progression#> .

#  The city's PRIVATE beliefs — a seller's terms, and nothing else.
#
#  It composed market:Hosting, actuation:Actuation and market:UniformPrice, so only those
#  modules' terms appear. No sensing block (its mains needs no witness), no desire, no
#  intention, no review: the city is what the supplier was before the barrel arcs — a
#  stakeless seller — kept deliberately, because one world now holds the whole ladder: a
#  stakeless seller, a dealer with a full BDI stack, and three pure buyers.

##  market:Hosting — how it runs a refill round
:city
    market:offerQuantityL 3.0 ;      # a refill lot: most of a barrel in one round
    market:reservePricePerL 0.05 ;   # mains water is cheap; the dealer's margin lives above this
    market:bidWindowS 3 ;            # how long it waits for bids before matching
    market:roundCooldownS 60 .       # it will not open rounds faster than this

##  actuation:Actuation — how long past a dose's own open-seconds it waits for the valve's
#   confirmation. A refill pours at mains pace, so the grace is slack on the report, not on
#   the water.
#  A PATIENCE, because the city wants something after all (#666's follow-on). Hosting a venue
#  means it can incur debts, and the market declares one desire for any agent that can: NO
#  OVERDUE DEBTS. That is a stake — met while every claim it issued still has time to run — and
#  the constitution holds an agent with a stake to stating how long it waits before deciding
#  again. 300 seconds, the supplier's, because they are the same kind of agent: a seller whose
#  only plans are about serving what it owes.
:city progression:patienceS 300 .
:city actuation:doseGraceS 10 .

##  How often it says how it is. Omit and the agent reports nothing; see orexis/metrics.py.
:city reporting:metricsIntervalS 60 .
